arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115-pro1x: add the rear camera module's EEPROM

The IMX582 module carries an 8 KiB EEPROM at 0x50 on the sensor's CCI
bus: its AWB ratios, a 17x13 lens shading table per Bayer channel,
autofocus and PDAF calibration, written at the factory for each unit.
With it described, at24 exposes it read-only as
/sys/bus/i2c/devices/2-0050/eeprom, and user space can correct the
lens's vignetting (corners at about a quarter of the centre).

CCI transfers are at most 8 bytes; regmap splits at24's reads to fit
the adapter's quirks.  The EEPROM answered with the camera off on the
phone (i2ctransfer, 2026-11-17), so VIO alone is given as its supply.

Not yet run on the phone.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
@@ -1012,6 +1012,14 @@ &cci_i2c0 {
 		vio-supply = <&vreg_l7p>;
 	};
 
+	/* rear module EEPROM: per-unit calibration (lens shading, AWB, AF) */
+	rear_eeprom: eeprom@50 {
+		compatible = "atmel,24c64";
+		reg = <0x50>;
+		read-only;
+		vcc-supply = <&vreg_l7p>;
+	};
+
 	rear_camera: camera@10 {
 		compatible = "sony,imx582";
 		reg = <0x10>;
